            <div xml:id="d566-a9">

                <pb facs="0788" n="682" xml:id="pg682"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 9.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">newfoundland.</hi></head>
                <p>Southern district, Middle Arm, to wit:</p>
                <p>The information and complaint of F. J. Bishop, master of the schooner <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Ernestine</hi>, of Burin, who saith:</p>
                <p>That early in November I had a fleet of nets set in the western passage of Wood’s
                    Island Harbor. I had them securely moored with a warp and ketch anchor belonging
                    to the schooner. The nets and moorings, valued at $60, were stolen by some
                    person or persons at present unknown. There was a large number of American and
                    Nova Scotian vessels at Wood’s Island. I have no suspicion of any person in
                    particular.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">F. J. Bishop.</hi></signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">Declared before me, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-11-25">this 25th day of November,
                    1905</date>.</dateline></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph O’Reilly</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >J. P. for Newfoundland.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
